{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The Shopping Spree", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "In the Groove", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe taste and style in music through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Making Comparisons", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"italic\">as</span> + adjective/adverb + <span class=\"italic\">as</span> to make comparisons when the things we are comparing are equal in some way:<br/><br/><span class=\"italic\">This leather jacket is <span class=\"strong\">as soft as</span> a sweater!</span><br/> <br/>You use comparative adjectives to compare yourself to another person.<br/>You use a superlative adjectives to compare yourself or something to a group of people.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use not <span class=\"italic\">as</span> ... <span class=\"italic\">as</span> to make comparisons between things which aren't equal:<br/><br/><span class=\"italic\">This leather jacket is<span class=\"strong\"> not as expensive as</span> that one.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can compare things using the words <span class=\"italic\">more (than)</span> or <span class=\"italic\">less (than)</span>. <br/>You can also use adjectives to compare things. Some    adjectives change to different words in the comparative and superlative form (<span class=\"italic\">good - better</span>, <span class=\"italic\">bad - worse</span>).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With one syllable words, you add <span class=\"italic\">-er</span> to the adjective to make the comparative form. You add <span class=\"italic\">-est</span> to the adjective to make the superlative form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With words of two or more syllables, you add the word <span class=\"italic\">more</span> before the adjective or adverb in the comparative form. You add <span class=\"italic\">the most</span> before the adjective or the adverb in the superlative form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I didn't think it was going to go <span class=\"strong\">as long as</span> it was.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It wasn't <span class=\"strong\">as deafening as</span> the one last year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The bands weren't <span class=\"strong\">as interesting as</span> the bands that played last year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Music Man parody was almost<span class=\"strong\"> as slick as</span> past musical productions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think I'd like to watch some <span class=\"strong\">older</span> Hollywood musicals this weekend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm not as well versed on names of <span class=\"strong\">the best</span> musicals as I should be though.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He's <span class=\"strong\">the biggest</span> movie buff. Besides, if there's food, he'll be more ecstatic!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Responses with <span class=\"italic\">So</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Neither</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"italic\">so</span> and <span class=\"italic\">neither</span> for positive and negative agreement.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">So</span> is used to show agreement with positive statements.  Sometimes we also use <span class=\"italic\">too</span> to express the same thing. Example:<br/><span class=\"strong\">Amanda</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I like this dress!</span></span><br/><span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: <span class=\"italic\">So do I. / I do too.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Neither</span> is used to show agreement with negative statements. Sometimes we also use <span class=\"italic\">either</span> to express the same thing. Example:<br/><span class=\"strong\">Amanda</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I don't think this fits well.</span><br/><span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: <span class=\"italic\">Neither do I. </span>(neither is a negative word)<br/><span class=\"italic\">I don't either. </span>(either is used with the negative)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use <span class=\"italic\">so</span> and <span class=\"italic\">neither</span>, the auxiliary needs to agree with the verb tense in the original statement.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A more colloquial form of negative agreement is <span class=\"italic\">Me too</span>. A more colloquial form of positive agreement is <span class=\"italic\">Me neither</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Positive agreement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I think I'd like to watch some old Hollywood musicals this weekend.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"So would I.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I think they could recommend some.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"So do I.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I could also look up some online.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"So could I.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"That would give us a list of as many movies as we could watch in an evening, I think.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"So do I.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative agreement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm not as well versed on names of musicals as I should be though.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Neither am I.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I really hate to go on about that music festival, but I wasn't at all happy with it!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Neither was I.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I wouldn't have shelled out all that cash on the tickets if I'd known.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I wouldn't have either.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't think we could have known though.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Neither do I.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Hollywood", "type": "name"}, {"content": "A place in the U.S. that is famous for making films", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'd like to watch some old Hollywood musicals this weekend. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about an event.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "well versed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to know a lot about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not as well versed in names of musicals as I should be though.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to shell out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give a large amount of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I wouldn't have shelled out all that cash on the tickets if I'd known.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "ta